WEBVTT

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
Once More to the Digital World

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
Insekimon's Rampage

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.930
Once More to the Digital World!

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.550
Insekimon's Rampage!

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:16.180
A Digimon researcher, Kurata, was once a member of the Digital World Exploration Squad.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.530
The Ultimate Level, SaberLeomon, appeared in the human world, causing destruction to the city.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:26.490
RiseGreymon fell in the face of such enormous power.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:31.510
But a mysterious Digimon suddenly appeared and saved them from danger.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.440
<i>The fact remains that you are a human.</i>

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.300
<i>You wouldn't understand the Digimon's suffering.</i>

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.930
I don't get why the Digiegg disappeared.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.410
That's not the only mystery around here.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:10.570
Hey!

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.080
Did you figure out its identity yet?

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.990
I re-examined the database, but I couldn't find anything related to it at all.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.550
Who'd have thought a completely unknown Digimon was around?

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.420
What's going on?

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.980
My, keep up the good work, everyone!

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:32.690
It's you!

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.790
Word has it that the transportation equipment is fixed.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:36.980
I didn't hear about this!

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.650
Why didn't you tell us?

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.600
We can't have you breaking it again when we finally got it fixed!

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.720
What?!

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.720
What?!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.160
Listen up, everyone.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:50.830
We will now be transporting Kurata-kun and these corps to the Digital World.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:54.590
This is an order from the Ministry of Confidentiality.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:57.120
Monster Appears

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:57.120
The Government Knew (Has Called for an Emergency Conference)

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.220
You've made a fine mess, letting these Digimon fool around.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.090
Just what is DATS doing?!

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.220
My apologies.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.350
We cannot let the Digimon get away with this behavior any longer.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:14.700
DATS will go at once to the Digital World and defeat Mercurimon, who is the cause behind all of this disorder!

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.510
Yes, sir, but...

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.100
What is it now?

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:22.320
Being of the Ultimate Level, Mercurimon holds immeasurable power.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.890
In order to oppose him on an equal level, we'll need time to come up with a detailed strategy...

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.790
There's no time for that!

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:31.760
We've already fallen into a state of warfare!

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.100
But...

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.420
In that case...

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.380
Why don't we consider discussing peace negotiations?

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:41.610
Well?

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:42.530
Kurata-kun!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:43.720
What are you doing here?

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.070
The other party is a Digimon.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:49.220
Do you really believe talking will get through to it?

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.460
You shouldn't be so prejudiced.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.900
Mercurimon is very intelligent,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.550
and it's quite likely that he can be persuaded through reason.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:58.150
But...

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:02.600
No one will be hurt if we settle this through peaceful negotiation.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:07.400
You, Governor Hashiba, will not have to take the blame for war, and we'll be able to come around to an easy solution.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.060
Mmm, it's all full of benefits as far as I can tell.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.090
Well?

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:13.540
That's...

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.660
Since you've argued to that extent, I'll leave you in charge.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.840
Make sure you've persuaded Mercurimon without fail.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:22.760
Huh?!

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:26.970
My, my!

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.360
I didn't think <i>I</i> 'd get personally involved in this business!

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.520
Governor Hashiba is quite rash!

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.520
But as it's come to this,

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.620
I will be your commander from now on.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:43.450
Please Digital Dive with us and act as our backup.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.430
Captain!

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.320
This is an order from the Ministry of Confidentiality.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:49.890
Gimme a break!

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:53.510
Why do we have to be ordered around by someone who isn't even in DATS?

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.940
That's right!

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.290
You've never even fought a Digimon before!

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.460
Don't try to blame this on me.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.380
Besides, I'm not necessarily doing this because I <i>want</i>  to.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:10.300
The Digimon on the other side have completely made us their enemies. We don't know when they'll come to attack us...

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.520
That's why I'm telling you to leave it all to us.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:19.310
Mercurimon's not the type of guy you can persuade through talking in the first place.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:20.520
The only thing that can get through to him...

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.230
are the fists of a passionate man!

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:30.050
I can't tell whether you're agreeing to help him or not...

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:34.830
It sounds like you're eager to go to the Digital World, but not to follow Kurata-san's orders.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:35.660
Wait, Masaru.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:36.720
Huh?

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.000
It's too soon.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.960
I'll have to re-adjust the pattern buffer to transfer this large number of people.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.920
Please give us one more day.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.900
In that case, there's no helping the situation.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.580
I understand. Very well.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.970
Then let's start over again tomorrow.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:57.930
Doctor Tohma.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.310
I foresee great things from you.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:02.500
Please take care of it.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.450
Master?

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:07.560
Your face is quite pale.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:08.280
I'm okay.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.620
Captain.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.410
Could there be another reason behind the Digital Dive?

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.240
I don't know what his true motives may be,

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.600
but this does not change the fact that our mission...

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.590
is to stop the fighting between our world and the Digital World.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.700
Don't forget that.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.520
Yes, sir.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.220
You're going to the Digital World?

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.780
Yeah.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.780
It might be difficult for you,

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:42.700
but we can't leave Mercurimon alone when there's the possibility he'll attack our world again.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:43.940
It's time for a return match!

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:45.810
Oh my.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:47.400
You're going back into danger again?

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:48.990
You can't!

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.180
Mercurimon really hates that humans come into Digital World.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.150
That's why...

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.330
You'll push him into war!

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:03.100
If we don't nip this in the bud quick, the sacrifices will just keep piling up...

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.290
for both the human world <i>and</i>  the Digital World!

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:07.460
I go, too!

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.130
To Mercurimon!

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.730
But if you're gonna go, who will you side with?

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.220
If you can't make a decision, stay here.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.270
You'll just make it harder on yourself.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.580
<i>Who will you side with?</i>

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.120
<i>If you can't make a decision, stay here.</i>

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.290
<i>You'll just make it harder on yourself.</i>

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:45.700
Ikuto.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:48.700
You can't sleep?

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:51.170
It's nothing.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.520
Is there... is there something the matter?

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:12.880
I was... remembering that man.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:13.950
That man?

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:17.120
The man who exchanged fists with me.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.640
That man...?

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.120
By "that man," you mean...?!

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:25.040
There wasn't the slightest bit of hesitation in his soul.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.260
When I felt that same Digisoul hit me,

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:30.270
my beliefs wavered.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:33.840
I've begun to wonder if not all humans are evil.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:37.300
Humans and Digimon are <i>not</i>  meant to interact with one another!

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:42.330
It's only natural that the humans who broke that rule are appropriately dealt with!

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:45.280
For many years...

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:49.480
So many years, I have served you, Mercurimon-sama.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:53.490
That is because I, too, earnestly wish for peace in the Digital World!

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:57.910
What is the matter?

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.350
I hear the humans' heartbeats.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:02.370
Have they...

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:03.830
Have they come here again?

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.160
An evil shadow is surrounding them.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:10.290
A shadow of deep hatred that intends to bury us alive.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:11.650
What?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.950
Please... please leave this situation to me!

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:14.980
Gotsumon.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:20.000
You are the only one who can protect the Digital World from the humans, Mercurimon-sama!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.150
Please don't forget that!

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:33.690
All right!

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.820
The transportation worked!

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.760
I see the scenery hasn't changed...

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:39.780
Professor Kurata!

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:43.030
There is no sign of a Digimon within one kilometer of this area!

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.110
That's wonderful.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.290
Now, let's get going.

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.570
Hey, wait up, old man!

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.300
Ikuto-kun!

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:55.670
Fal-chan!

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.760
I've made snacks!

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:01.890
Where's Ikuto-kun?

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.970
He said he's not hungry.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:08.810
What's wrong?

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.240
 Could you be scared of seeing Mercurimon again?

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:22.540
Mercurimon doesn't forgive traitors...

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:23.740
He won't forgive me...

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.070
That's not true!

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:29.570
You're important to Mercurimon...

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:31.500
But I'm human.

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:36.720
My body... human...

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.360
But my heart... Digimon...

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:41.760
What should I do?!

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:46.560
Just you wait, Mercurimon!

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:50.200
My fists will send along the message of my soul to you!

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:52.990
That's just a fancy way of saying "punch his lights out," isn't it?

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:53.590
Yep.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:54.890
You don't get it, do you?

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:58.450
Stuff like words is useless between men.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:10:59.900
I found a Digimon signal!

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.570
It's heading towards us at rapid speed!

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:04.530
H-Here it comes!

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.240
That's...

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:08.850
Go home!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.000
Go home, you wretched humans!

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:15.900
We've come to talk!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.960
We request an audience with Mercurimon-san!

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:20.710
I won't!

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:23.250
I won't fall for that!

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:27.210
You plan to catch him off guard and leave Mercurimon-sama for dead, right?!

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:28.390
Come on out, Zudomon!

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:41.190
Zudomon

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:41.190
Perfect Level

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:33.800
Zudomon.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:37.670
A Perfect Level Digimon who has a Thor hammer made out of Chrome Digizoid.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:41.190
Wielding it with his sinewy muscles, it brings forth his special attack, Hammer Spark.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:42.880
It's here!

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:46.550
Retreat!

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:47.990
Protect Professor Kurata!

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.760
Looks like we really can't get there that easily!

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.050
Let's go, Aniki!

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:53.210
Yeah!

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:55.360
They're taking his attack head-on...

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.420
As usual, they're not acting on any strategy whatsoever.

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:03.690
Baby Flame!

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:09.180
What?!

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:12.370
Masaru!

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:17.990
Agumon!

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:19.060
You okay?

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:20.010
Aniki!

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.530
It's pitch-black!

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:22.780
You're hopeless.

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.810
All members take cover! Take cover!

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.700
Now, it's your job to handle things from here!

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.550
Good luck!

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.160
It's dark!

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:35.740
It's dark!

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:37.430
Someone help me!

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:39.000
This is kind of the worst.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:39.920
Here he comes!

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.960
Ow! Don't hit me with a mallet!

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.190
Let's go, Gaomon!

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.150
Yes, Master!

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.290
Digisoul...

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:08.640
Full Charge!

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:13.790
Gaomon, evolve!

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:25.740
MachGaogamon!

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:27.220
Go!

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:35.730
What?

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.810
What are you doing?

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.360
You're losing!

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.580
Oh, shut up.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:47.910
Let's go, Lalamon.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:48.660
Okay!

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:50.670
Digisoul...

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:56.290
Full Charge!

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.540
Lalamon, evolve!

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:15.180
Lilamon!

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:17.350
Marvel Shot!

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:24.400
Gaoga Tornado!

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:41.190
Impressive.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.530
But, as long as I'm here...

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:47.840
you won't lay a finger on Mercurimon-sama!

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:49.440
Gotsumon!

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:51.840
You're not strong enough to take us on your own!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.800
Just let us pass!

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:55.660
I wonder about that!

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.270
Let me show you...

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.230
my true form!

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:09.760
It can't be...

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.990
Is Gotsumon evolving?

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:18.760
Ikuto-kun! Fal-chan!

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:19.820
I'm coming in.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:26.270
Oh? Where did they go?

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:30.090
Huh?

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.310
The weather's gotten nicer.

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:48.820
Whenever Masaru was worried about something, he'd always come up here and look at the sky, too.

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:52.900
You two... are very alike.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.030
Want to talk about it?

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.510
Gotsumon, evolve!

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.330
Insekimon!

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:13.010
...He just changed color.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:22.480
Insekimon

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:22.480
Perfect Level

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:15.060
Insekimon.

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:17.600
The Perfect Level Digimon that evolves from Gotsumon.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:19.730
His special attack is Cosmo Flash.

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:22.480
With his hands, he shoots down energy he collects from the universe.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:25.320
I'm completely different on the inside.

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:26.460
Have a look!

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.600
Just what...?

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.360
That's a colossal amount of energy!

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.670
Cosmo Flash!

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.580
Well? What do you think about my power now?

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:43.620
Hold it!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.250
Don't forget about me!

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:51.210
Digisoul...

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:56.700
Full Charge!

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:00.760
Aniki!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.040
Agumon, evolve!

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:14.130
RiseGreymon!

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:15.880
It's useless.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.730
Solid Strike!

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:20.140
He disappeared?

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:22.360
No way!

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:23.330
Where...?

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:27.150
You're not as strong as I expected!

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:30.940
What's going on?

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.400
He can disappear!

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.970
He's not disappearing.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.910
He's moving at super-speed!

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.760
Even I can't see how fast he is!

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:44.600
You can't catch my movements!

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:47.060
Now, here I come!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.860
Humans and Digimon, huh?

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:58.330
What should I do?

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.640
I'm sorry.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.590
I don't know.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:09.140
Because, you're the only one who understand the feelings of both the humans and the Digimon, Ikuto-kun.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.500
Feelings of both...

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:16.460
What do you want to do?

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:18.970
I...

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:26.340
How about that!

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:27.600
Have you learned your lesson?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.610
We have to seal his movements somehow.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:36.280
I could paralyze him with my Un Deux Pollen...

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:40.670
But if we can't see him, we can't attack at the right moment.

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:42.530
If we could at least detect his position...

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:43.740
That's right!

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:47.810
When he punches, he should be within reach!

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:49.170
RiseGreymon!

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.320
I see!

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.770
I got it, Aniki!

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:54.560
Your show of courage is painful to watch.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:01.800
There!

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:05.700
All right!

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.310
Unbelievable.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:08.720
You're using too much brute force.

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:10.690
Let go of me!

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:13.500
Un Deux Pollen!

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:19.860
Th-This is... my body is...!

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.570
Winning Knuckle!

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:27.450
Did they get him?

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.700
No... that's...

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:34.670
You've entertained me quite a bit,

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:38.030
but playtime is over now.

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:40.310
All of you will disappear!

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.760
Cosmo Fla-!

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:49.440
Rising Destroyer!

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:51.180
What?!

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:59.030
Mercurimon-sama!

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:05.170
Bravo, bravo!

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:09.080
That's just what I expected from you, DATS members!

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.620
Things have gotten quite interesting.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:15.630
Are you sure about this, Ikuto?

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:18.290
Yeah. I want to stop the fight.

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:22.590
Ikuto.

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:26.330
I...

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.800
go to the Digital World.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:38.190
You're here.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.280
Stay back, everyone.

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:48.420
We'll solve this with a man-to-man fight!

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:49.740
Wait, you were being serious?

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:00.520
Mercurimon!

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.600
I've come to finish this!

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:04.130
Is that you, Daimon Masaru?

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:06.580
Yeah! No need for anymore words!

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.450
The answer will show itself through our fists!

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.470
That's being a man!

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:10.980
Hmph.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:13.560
You can't fight what's in your blood, is it?

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.480
We may have been destined to meet like this.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.100
Here I come!

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:24.810
Stop!!!

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:33.820
Ikuto?

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:33.820
Ikuto?

